            <ArticleTitle>[Re-evaluation of the application of procedure for prolapse and hemorrhoids in the last 15 years].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1211-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Procedure for prolapse and hemorrhoids( PPH) is one of the important techniques developed for the treatment of hemorrhoids with severe degree in the last decade. Its principle is based on the &quot;anal cushion&quot; theory.Compared with traditional hemorrhoidectomy , PPH has advantages of shorter operation time , minor degree of postoperative pain , shorter hospital stay and quicker recovery.However, the occurrence of relapse and re-prolapse of hemorrhoids is high. Besides, the short-term efficacy of PPH for the constipation outlet obstruction caused by anterior rectocele is also favorable.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
